---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: ""
description: "Haha Systems Research"
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---
<div class="home wrap">
  <section class="home__hero" aria-labelledby="home-lede">
    <p class="home__sub">haha-systems / index</p>
    <h1 id="home-lede" class="home__lede">
      <strong>Haha Systems</strong>
    </h1>
    <em class="home__section-title">All the world's a stage, and we are merely players.</em>
    <p class="home__section-title">Research on intelligence, symbiosis, and the systems we build.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="home__sections" aria-label="Sections">
    {% for s in site.sections %}
      {% set entries = collections[s.slug] | sortByDateDesc %}
      <article class="home__section">
        <h2 class="home__section-title">
          <a href="{{ ('/' + s.slug + '/') | url }}">{{ s.title }}</a>
          <span class="home__count">{{ entries.length }}</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="home__section-blurb">{{ s.blurb }}</p>
        <div class="home__recent">
          {% if entries.length %}
            {% for item in entries | limit(3) %}
              <a href="{{ item.url | url }}">
                <span>{{ item.data.date | readableDate }}</span>
                &nbsp;·&nbsp;
                <span>{{ item.data.title }}</span>
              </a>
            {% endfor %}
          {% else %}
            <span class="home__recent-empty">— empty</span>
          {% endif %}
        </div>
      </article>
    {% endfor %}
  </section>

  <p class="home__colophon">
    Built in plain Markdown and Eleventy. No tracking. No newsletter. Updates appear
    when there is something to record. Source organized by section; each entry is a
    file on disk.
  </p>
</div>
